Understanding what you are protecting is a prerequisite for effective security work. This register captures the assets, or things of value, associated with your product or system.

[TIP]
====
*Where does an asset belong?* If it is part of the product, model it in the threat model {{#report}}"name":"secdeva/reports/xref","identifier":"secdeva_document_threat-model"{{/report}}. If it is part of how you *build, ship or run* the product, create it here.

The processes, interfaces and data stores of the threat model appear in the list below automatically. Record the categories of data each of them holds — including cryptographic keys, credentials and personal data — directly on those elements.

Record the overall criticality of each asset — it tells you where to spend your security effort first. If it is not obvious, rate the criticality of confidentiality, integrity, availability, and health, safety and the environment; the overall criticality is then derived as the highest of the ones you rate.

Use the *asset criticality requirement* field of this register to choose whether recording the criticality is optional, whether the overall criticality is required for each asset, or whether all of the criticality fields are required.
